    <string name="help_tiers">Privilege tiers</string>
    <string name="tier_base">Base</string>
    <string name="tier_base_body">Public Android APIs only. Works on every phone with no setup.</string>
    <string name="tier_adb">ADB</string>
    <string name="tier_adb_body">Grant extra read permissions once with adb from a computer.</string>
    <string name="tier_shizuku">Shizuku</string>
    <string name="tier_shizuku_body">Shell-level reads through the Shizuku app, without a computer.</string>
    <string name="tier_root">Root</string>
    <string name="tier_root_body">Full read access on rooted phones.</string>
    <string name="tier_active">Active</string>
    <string name="tier_planned">Planned</string>
    <string name="help_privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_1">No internet permission: nothing leaves the phone unless you share a report yourself.</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_2">No trackers, ads, analytics or Google Play Services.</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_3">Read-only: Droynis opens Settings for you but never changes anything itself.</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_4">Reports leave out hardware identifiers, phone numbers and account names.</string>
    <string name="help_faq">Questions and answers</string>
    <string name="faq_q1">Does a score of 100 mean my phone is safe?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">No. Droynis checks the settings that public Android APIs can see. It cannot find malware, spyware hidden in system apps or tampered firmware. A high score means the basics are in place.</string>
    <string name="faq_q2">Why are some checks Unknown?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">Android hides some settings from apps, and some vendors change or remove them. Droynis then says it does not know instead of guessing. Android 17, for example, can report USB debugging and developer options as off to every app.</string>
    <string name="faq_q3">Why does Droynis need to see all installed apps?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">Since Android 11 apps see only a few other apps by default. Without the “query all packages” permission the app checks would miss most apps and pass falsely.</string>
    <string name="faq_q4">Can Droynis fix problems for me?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">No, on purpose. It explains what to change and opens the right Settings screen, so you stay in control of every change.</string>
    <string name="faq_q5">What is a privilege tier?</string>
    <string name="faq_a5">Each check states the access it needs. This version uses only the Base tier, so every check works on any phone without root, Shizuku or adb.</string>
    <string name="faq_q6">Does Droynis run in the background?</string>
    <string name="faq_a6">No. It scans only while it is open: no background services, notifications or wakelocks.</string>
